<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--25-25-25">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        <h2 class="article-list--heading">Understanding predefined reports</h2>
        <p class="article-list--desc">Predefined reports help you quickly get started with Insights. Each report automatically populates with a set of common <a href="/app-store/help/reporting/0023-reporting-options-and-definitions">metrics and dimensions</a>, but you can always make changes to the configuration to best support your needs. There are two kinds of predefined reports: Performance and Advanced.</p>

		

        

        <ul role="list" class="">
             <li role="listitem">
    <strong>Performance</strong>
    <p>These reports include common views of your performance across various dimensions including: Campaign Groups, Campaigns, Ad Groups, Ads, Keywords, Search Terms, Ad Placements, and Country or Region. With these reports, you can view and compare data across your entire account, helping you gain a better understanding of what’s doing well and what might need more attention.</p>    
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
    <strong>Advanced</strong>
    <p>These reports show aggregate data that can be helpful to your advertising efforts, but is not necessarily linked to any specific campaign. For example, the Impression Share reports can help you understand your competitiveness on search terms by country or region, including your impression share on a search term, your rank compared to other advertisers, and the search term’s popularity in the country or region.</p>    
</li>
        </ul>           

		

    </section>

 

    
    
</div>
<section class="article-copy-block margin-bottom--25-25-25">










































    
        
        
  
        
        







    
        

        

 		
		
		


        


		


		

		


        

        

        
		
					
                    
        






   

    
        
        
  
        
        







    
        

        

 		
		
		


        


		


		

		


        

        

        
		
					
                    
        






   

    
        
        
  
        
        







    
        

        

 		
		
		


        


		


		

		


        

        

        
		
					
                    <p class="article-copy-block--description ">Each predefined report is only a starting point. You have the ability to customize and configure the report to your liking by editing the metrics, dimensions, date range, and applying filters to simplify the data further. Note that certain reports, such as the Impression Share reports have some restrictions on dimensions that can’t be edited, such as the timezone.<br class="br-l br-m br-s no-space" /><br class="br-l br-m br-s no-space" />
If you’d like to save, save as, share, download or delete the report, click the Save button or the More button (three dots) in the upper-right corner.</p>
        






   

    
        
        
  
        
        








 	
    

	


	


        

         

        



		

        

        

     
     

    

    

    







   

    
        
        
  
        
        






    
    
    
    
    
    
    
        
        
    
        
      
    






   

    

































