<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--25-25-25">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        <h2 class="article-list--heading">View and manage existing reports</h2>
        <p class="article-list--desc">On the Insights landing page, you’ll see all the reports you’ve created, that have been shared with you, and any that you created using Custom Reports that were transferred to Insights. From the landing page you can:</p>

		

    </section>

 

    
    
</div>
<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--25-25-25">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        <h3 class="article-list--heading">Review report modifications</h3>
        <p class="article-list--desc">By default, reports on the Insights page are sorted in order of when they were last opened. You can also see and sort by report name, creation date, and by who created it.</p>

		

    </section>

 

    
    
</div>
<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--25-25-25">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        <h3 class="article-list--heading">Edit an existing report</h3>
        <p class="article-list--desc">If you created the report originally, you can make changes to it. Otherwise, changes or edits you make to it won’t be saved unless you save as your own version. To open a report, simply click the report name on the Insights landing page or click the button with the three dots in the Actions column.</p>

		

    </section>

 

    
    
</div>
<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--25-25-25">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        <h3 class="article-list--heading">Download a report</h3>
        <p class="article-list--desc">In the Actions column on the Insights landing page, click the download icon next to the report. You can download the report as an XLSX file.</p>

		

    </section>

 

    
    
</div>
<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--25-25-25">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        <h3 class="article-list--heading">More actions</h3>
        <p class="article-list--desc">In the Actions column on the Insights landing page, click the button with the three dots to share, save as, or delete a report. Reports are shared to campaign groups. Anyone with access to the campaign group will get access to the report. You can only delete reports that you own, and deleting them will permanently delete the report for you and remove access to anyone that belonged to a campaign group that you had shared it with.</p>

		

    </section>

 

    
    
</div>
<div class="helparticlelist margin-bottom--50">
 

 



    

    

    
	    

    <section class="article-list">

        <h2 class="article-list--heading">Troubleshooting in Insights</h2>
        <p class="article-list--desc">Certain combinations of metrics and dimensions may cause issues with your report generation. When creating reports, keep in mind that:</p>

		

        

        <ul role="list" class="">
             <li role="listitem">
	You can’t combine more than one Time dimension in a single report.   
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
	All reports have an 24-month date range limit.   
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
	For data to be readable, Impression Share, Search Popularity, and Rank measures must be used with Day, App, App ID, Country or Region, and Search Term dimensions.   
</li>
        
             <li role="listitem">
	Predefined Impression Share reports can only display the last 12 weeks of data.   
</li>
        </ul>           

		

    </section>

 

    
    
